& [CoreInsight] is conservation plus transformation plus accountable articulation
  + Scribe is the conserving pole that anchors before-state, source, context, lineage, and durable result
  + Refiner is the transforming pole that sharpens or changes an already-present semantic structure only under an explicit purpose and contract
  + Cantor is the repeatable logical process that carries a subject from one inscribed state through a bounded refinement into another inscribed state with the delta, judgments, proof, uncertainty, and reentry position exposed
  + articulation is the visible projection of that complete transition rather than mere fluent wording
  = compact: Cantor faithfully transforms recorded meaning into a new recorded semantic state

& [PrimalFormCandidate] is an inscription-refinement-inscription recurrence
  + [B] is the immutable before-state and its source lineage
  + [P] is the active purpose
  + [K] is the governing meaning, authority, evidence, and effect contract
  + [R] is one admitted refinement or semantic operation over B under P and K
  + [B_prime] is the immutable after-state
  + [Delta] is the exact change from B to B_prime
  + [J] is the classified judgment set
  + [Proof] is sources, rules, evidence, authority, and validation
  + [Residual] is uncertainty, disagreement, omission, fault, or unresolved frontier
  + [Recurrence] is the next transition may use B_prime only after the prior transition is inscribed and admitted
  = compact: `C<B,P,K> := S(B) -> R(B|P,K) -> S(B',Delta,J,Proof,Residual)`
  = operational: ANCHOR -> REFINE -> INSCRIBE -> REENTER

& [PrimalVersusFacultyDelineation] prevents circular architecture
  + [PrimalScribe] is the kernel obligation to preserve exact semantic state and lineage around every transition
  + [PrimalRefiner] is the kernel obligation to apply only an admitted, bounded, inspectable semantic transformation
  + [ScribeFaculty] is a compiled specialist program emphasizing memory, provenance, revision, and reentry through those primitives
  + [RefinerFaculty] is a compiled specialist program restricted to sharpening already-formed structure without semantic invention
  + [Cantor] executes the primal process on which faculty programs themselves depend
  = must: derive the Scribe and Refiner faculty programs from the primal obligations rather than make the engine depend on its own faculty library
  - never: collapse the existing restricted Refiner faculty into every inference, planning, composition, or effect operation

& [ExistingImplementationResonance] is direct but not yet identity authority
  + SemanticTransition already contains immutable before_state, history_review, instruction, judgments, after_state, effect_events, faults, and trace
  + TransitionTrace already carries source, rule, reason, evidence, authority, and uncertainty
  + the evaluator already returns one complete transition after applying one Instruction
  + protocol proof and continuation already expose result binding and finish, query-or-reframe, or stop
  + this is a concrete manifestation of the proposed primal form even though it was not previously named as Cantor's defining Scribe-Refiner recurrence
  = should: test whether existing SemanticTransition is the primal form before inventing a duplicate machine type

& [FacultyAndAgentBoundary] remains intact
  + Observer selects, coordinates, reviews, reconciles, continues, or stops transitions; Observer is governor rather than the primal transform itself
  + Honesty and Security are non-optional gates when truth, authority, disclosure, or effects are consequential
  + Planner, Weaver, inference operators, models, humans, and tools may propose or perform specialized transformations whose results reenter the primal Cantor process
  + Shaliach is the commissioned agent that uses Cantor under a principal's mandate and remains distinct from the semantic process
  + EffectBroker alone commits authorized exterior effects
  - never: infer that reducing Cantor's logical identity to a primal process eliminates governance, deliberation, agency, or effect boundaries

& [NoNewMeaningBoundary] resolves the Refiner tension
  + the existing Refiner faculty cannot create a missing conclusion or change semantic boundaries while compressing
  + PrimalRefiner may apply an already-declared semantic Instruction, but the instruction's result must classify whether it preserves, derives, proposes, revises, imports, or effects meaning
  + formal derivation is admissible only with its premises and rule preserved
  + model or human novelty enters as attributed candidate material rather than as self-originated Cantor authority
  + semantic revision requires explicit revision authority and cannot be disguised as compression
  = must: preserve the operation class so transformation is never laundered as equivalence-preserving refinement

& [ArchitecturalConsequences] are simplifying if the candidate survives SJS
  + compile, query, inspect, reflect, deliberate, learn, and embodied-agent operations can share one transition waist
  + every operation begins from admitted inscribed state and ends in a proof-bearing inscribed state or visible fault
  + the semantic database becomes the durable Scribe surface while deterministic execution and bounded projections become Refiner surfaces
  + learned routing may propose which refinement to apply but cannot bypass inscription, contracts, gates, or proof
  + reentry becomes recurrence from an admitted after-state rather than prompt-history imitation
  + Cantor's chant becomes the repeated faithful articulation of these transitions

& [CandidateRequirementSet] is CPI-001 through CPI-010
  + [CPI-001] is define Cantor's primal identity as a repeatable inscription-refinement-inscription semantic process
  + [CPI-002] is bind every transition to before-state, purpose, governing contract, and source lineage
  + [CPI-003] is classify the applied operation as preserve, derive, propose, revise, import, or effect-bearing
  + [CPI-004] is emit after-state, exact delta, judgments, proof, residual uncertainty, faults, and continuation
  + [CPI-005] is permit recurrence only from an admitted inscribed after-state
  + [CPI-006] is define Scribe and Refiner faculties as programs over primal obligations without circular dependency
  + [CPI-007] is preserve Observer governance, Honesty and Security gates, Shaliach agency, and EffectBroker separation
  + [CPI-008] is test reuse or revision of existing SemanticTransition before adding a new machine form
  + [CPI-009] is forbid semantic novelty, authority, or effects from being laundered as refinement
  + [CPI-010] is prove verbose, compact, machine, and human articulation remain semantically equivalent

& [OpenQuestions] require SJS rather than intuitive closure
  + whether the formal sequence is Scribe then Refiner then Scribe or one continuous coupled operation
  + whether primal articulation is exactly SemanticTransition, a stricter profile over it, or a more primitive IR beneath it
  + whether `Refiner` is the right primitive name given the narrower existing faculty contract
  + which current Cantor identity specifications this candidate clarifies, supersedes, or merely explains
  + whether query results that do not mutate SemanticState still form transitions through a projection state
  + how primal form identity is content-addressed and compiled from SOP without duplicating existing protocol proof

& [Decision] is preserve and process as a core-identity clarification candidate
